From 1ac6a9ea2f58a64fc2c4c5ccd0b68fec70fed994 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 03:07:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: live bitrates and demux queue levels in the player
 information

Kodi 22 publishes Player.Process(videolivebitrate, audiolivebitrate,
videoqueuelevel, audioqueuelevel), but Estuary shows none of them. On
the player tab, show the bitrate actually read for video and audio in
the free fourth row of the right column, and how full the video and
audio packet queues are next to the cache level, so that a stutter from
a slow source (a streaming add-on) can be told from a rendering one.

The idea comes from CoreELEC's player information; its dialog is not
taken over, since most of it reads CoreELEC-specific labels. Strings
31676-31678 follow the Hades range 31650-31675, with Spanish
translations.
---
 .../resource.language.en_gb/strings.po         | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../resource.language.es_ar/strings.po         | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../resource.language.es_es/strings.po         | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../resource.language.es_mx/strings.po         | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../xml/DialogPlayerProcessInfo.xml            | 13 +++++++++++--
 5 files changed, 83 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

